# Core rules

- Read `AGENT_CONTEXT.md` before changing behavior or architecture.
- Keep temporary plans, investigations, reviews, and architecture drafts under `ai/dev/` only.
- Never commit credentials, tokens, chat contents, user exports, or production identifiers.
- Do not present planned Telegram, moderation, persistence, or AI behavior as implemented.
- Preserve the separation between app construction in `src/app.ts` and network startup in
  `src/server.ts` so tests do not bind ports.
- Prefer small domain modules with explicit inputs over access to global environment or SDK clients.
